Vintage illustration of a master craftsman's wooden workbench viewed from above, featuring an intricate arrangement of ornate puzzle pieces in warm mahogany and brass tones, each piece uniquely carved with gears, cogs, and mechanical details that interlock perfectly together. Some pieces float slightly above the surface as if being assembled by invisible hands. Scattered around are antique drafting tools—compasses, rulers, and small precision instruments with aged patina. Warm amber light streams from an oil lamp at the corner, casting long shadows across the weathered wood grain. The composition suggests the satisfying moment of modular components clicking into place, creating something greater than the sum of parts. Sepia and golden undertones dominate with touches of deep burgundy and forest green in the mechanical details.
